  "notes": "University Park. Built from the real archived 2025-26 bulletin (https://bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2025-2026/undergraduate/colleges/engineering/computer-engineering-bs/), raw HTML fetched and cross-checked against the page's own printed credit subtotals (128-129 total). Course-for-course and semester-for-semester identical to CMPEN-2024.json's Suggested Academic Plan (diffed byte-for-byte -- zero differences). Program Requirements course list, entrance-to-major GPA (3.20, unchanged), and the enumerated CMPEN-elective list (CMPEN 411/416/417/454/455/471/472/473/475 + EE 453/456 -- still no CMPEN 462) are all unchanged from 2024-25, i.e. the pre-overhaul curriculum held through the entire 2022-23 to 2025-26 span with only the two administrative-enrollment-control changes noted in the 2022/2023 files' notes. IMPORTANT DISCOVERY while building this file: the live bulletin page now shown at CMPEN-2026.json's own 'source' URL is the 2026-27 edition, and its Program Requirements tab (raw HTML confirmed, not a WebFetch artifact -- verified inside the page's own id=\"programrequirementstexttab\" div) has been substantially overhauled relative to every year 2022-23 through 2025-26 covered by this file and its siblings: CMPSC 150N (Computing and Society) added as a new prescribed course, CMPSC 122/132 replaced by CMPSC 222 (Advanced Data Structures and Algorithms in C), CMPSC 311 and CMPSC 473 replaced by CMPSC 315 + CMPSC 316 (Computer Systems I/II), the ECON 102/104 requirement removed entirely, MATH 220 and MATH 250 dropped from the prescribed list, and the stated Requirements-for-the-Major total fell from 110 credits to 106-108 (overall degree minimum 127, down from 128). However, that same live page's Suggested Academic Plan tab (id=\"suggestedacademicplantexttab\") still shows the OLD, pre-overhaul course sequence verbatim -- identical to this file's own semesters, including ECON 102/104, CMPSC 122/132, CMPSC 311, CMPSC 473, MATH 220, MATH 250, and the 128-129 total -- meaning the two tabs of PSU's own live 2026-27 CMPEN bulletin page currently contradict each other. This file (2025-26, archived) is unaffected by that discrepancy since it's built from a distinct, internally-consistent archived edition. But it means CMPEN-2026.json itself may need re-verification/rebuild against the new Program Requirements tab before a future CMPEN-2027.json is built -- flagged for a separate, dedicated pass; out of this task's authorized scope (Part 2 of this build only permits editing CMPEN-2026.json's campus field/notes for a genuine campus-availability finding, not for general course-content staleness), so this is reported here and in this build's own summary output instead.",
